# TO CHECK STATUS OF mbatchd
Just like we run "lsf_daemons status" and it gives us running status of lim,res and sbatchd. For getting status of mbtachd is not direct you can 
indirectly check its status by running:-
Method1: commands "bhosts" and "bqueues". If it returns your cluster host list and queues normally, mbatchd is up and running.
If it throws an error like batch system daemon not responding, mbatchd is down or hung.
Method2: ps auxfww | grep mbatchd
Method3: badmin mbdhist
         badmin showstatus

# TO CHECK STATUS OF pim
If lim is running successfully on a host, pim should automatically be running right alongside it.
ps auxfww | grep pim

